  "description": "SlideRule is the spec contract: the fluent API an architecture spec is written in, and the rule model it builds. It is the only SlideRule package a spec project needs. A spec declares layers, rules and scopes. A rule is either the law (Enforce) or a ratchet over a counted baseline (Migrate). A scope either fails a new reference into it (Quarantine) or only warns when a change touches it (Caution). Checking comes from the sliderule tool (SlideRule.Cli), the build analyzer (SlideRule.Analyzers) and the xUnit adapter (SlideRule.Xunit), and rendering from the tool. The package includes a Roslyn analyzer that reports a spec's bad string literals as compiler warnings while the spec is written. It also includes a completion provider that offers the referenced projects' namespaces and type names in the editor. This package is netstandard2.0 with zero dependencies, so a spec project can target anything from net48 up.",
